  "notes": [
    "Reflexive -AR verb with a spelling change: *z→c* before *e*, to preserve the soft sound — affects the yo form of Pretérito Indefinido (*me tranquilicé*, not *me tranquilizé*) and all of Subjuntivo Presente (*me tranquilice, te tranquilices...*)",
    "Same spelling pattern as *cruzar* (crucé, cruce) — no stem change involved, just the orthographic z→c swap",
    "Affirmative imperative attaches the reflexive pronoun with a written accent to preserve the original stressed syllable: *tranquilízate, tranquilícese, tranquilicémonos, tranquilícense*; negative imperative keeps the pronoun separate: *no te tranquilices*...",
    "Past participle: *tranquilizado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to calm down\" or \"to relax (oneself)\" — *tranquilízate, todo va a salir bien* (calm down, everything's going to be fine)",
    "Base verb *tranquilizar* (non-reflexive, \"to calm/reassure someone else\") is the transitive counterpart: *el médico la tranquilizó* (the doctor reassured her)",
    "Related: *tranquilo/a* (calm, adj.), *tranquilidad* (calmness, peace of mind), *tranquilizante* (tranquilizer, sedative)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/t/Tranquilizarse.md"
